   "subtitle": "Korean · Chinese · Japanese · English code-switching",
   "desc": "Each sentence mixes a matrix language with embedded foreign / borrowed words. These examples are chosen so that PhARO pronounces every part of the sentence — both the embedded foreign word and the surrounding matrix language — at least as accurately as (and usually better than) all three commercial systems, checked segment-by-segment rather than only on the whole-utterance average (PFER; lower is better).",
